ggregate prediction error than the evaluated random-acquisition low-rank and greedy-coverage ridge pipelines, including on never-queryable audit targets, but the advantage is not uniform across held-out splits and does not isolate the contribution of mixtures or value-adaptive acquisition.\nnarrative_rationale : The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation and its row/checkpoint records, not the search ordering or unverified internal diagnostics: these support direct error-versus-budget comparisons, common-target audits, an adverse family-disjoint split, and a historical-column permutation control. One shared question covers two split conditions on a single pinned embedding benchmark source; these are not independent datasets. The paper is an empirical method-integration study with explicit limits, not a new-architecture claim, a universal benchmark-compression result, or a campaign report. Final qualification is independently reported as completed/qualified by final.qualification.status\nprior_paper_story_status : rejected\nedit_framing_decision : Not an edit-mode run: previous_paper, staged new/old programs, aggregated, extra_tasks, contributions.md, and instantiated edit-context files are absent. Rejected means no inherited manuscript story is adopted, not that an existing manuscript was evaluated and rejected. Preserve-the-prior-story is inapplicable; broadening the source brief to generative language models is unsupported; recentering on the latest quadrature branch is unsupported. Select the frozen evaluated latent-model family, with the two split conditions as evidence blocks under one thesis.\nstaged_input_impact : length=5\nmethod_groups : length=5\nresults_focus : length=7\nfigure_plan : length=4\nfigure_specs : length=3\nsupplementary_plan : keys=['purpose', 'planned_subsections']\nforbidden_headings : length=10\nforbidden_phrases : length=21\nnotes_for_writer : length=20\nfailure_reason : \n\nFILE paper_data.json ROOT dict\nablation_studies :