issingness-aware latent-model procedure predict an unseen embedding model’s recorded but unqueried benchmark scores at small query budgets, and how does this change under name-proxy-family-disjoint evaluation and destroyed historical cross-task alignment?\",\n7:  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation and its row/checkpoint records, not the search ordering or unverified internal diagnostics: these support direct error-versus-budget comparisons, common-target audits, an adverse family-disjoint split, and a historical-column permutation control. One shared question covers two split conditions on a single pinned embedding benchmark source; these are not independent datasets. The paper is an empirical method-integration study with explicit limits, not a new-architecture claim, a universal benchmark-compression result, or a campaign report. Final qualification is independently reported as completed/qualified by final.qualification.status and final.qualification.outcome; that administrative outcome is not evidence of universal validity, superiority, or mechanistic attribution.\",\n9:  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not an edit-mode run: previous_paper, staged new/old programs, aggregated, extra_tasks, contributions.md, and instantiated edit-context files are absent. Rejected means no inherited manuscript story is adopted, not that an existing manuscript was evaluated and rejected. Preserve-the-prior-story is inapplicable; broadening the source brief to generative language models is unsupported; recentering on the latest quadrature branch is unsupported. Select the frozen evaluated latent-model family, with the two split conditions as evidence blocks under one thesis.\",\n14:    \"The final evidence contains model-group and name-proxy-family-disjoint conditions, original/permuted historical-score arms, and a zero-weight reset replay. Those measured conditions set the scope, rather than the broader generative-model aspiration in the original brief.\",\n31:      \"include_reason\": \"The stronger evaluated comparator uses overlap-shrunk historical correlations for coverage and ridge prediction. Retain its adverse-to-proposed family-disjoint split; it is a whole-pipeline comparator, not a matched predictor control.\"\n34:      \"name\": \"Historical per-benchmark mean\",\n46:    \"Make the common-target view central: eight panel-level audit columns are never queryable, with at least four recorded audit cells per held-out row. Derive fixed-audit MAE by method, budget, split condition, and seed from final.evidence.episodes; retain the evaluator’s row versus family weighting. Descriptive all-condition audit means derived from recorded case summaries are 0.02687114697690909 for the proposed procedure, 0.029409541552239845 for greedy ridge, and 0.0354685223509185 for random low-rank. Label these as derived summaries, not extra runs.\",\n48:    \"Expose heterogeneity in the main text and a six-row split-by-seed comparison table: in the family-disjoint seed 4021, proposed remaining-target MAE is 0.03665795350948428 versus greedy ridge 0.03414373962951742; fixed-audit MAE is 0.02971584244781457 versus greedy ridge 0.026874009322976657. These are evidence of nonuniform comparative performance, not a diagnosed validity failure.\",\n72:      \"allow_progression\": false,\n83:        \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/program.py\",\n84:        \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/mixture.py\"\n96:      \"split_by\": \"model-group versus name-proxy-family-disjoint holdout\",\n100:      \"allow_progression\": false,\n108:      \"aggregation\": \"Exclude replay and permuted arms. At each checkpoint aggregate observations.audit_mae or baselines[method].audit_mae across rows; model-group uses equal row weights, family-disjoint uses equal family means; then average equally over the three seeds. Plot the three aggregate seed values as unconnected small points in the method color and one descriptive mean curve, not as additional method series. The horizontal axis is evaluation budget, not campaign progress.\",\n119:      \"split_by\": \"model-group versus name-proxy-family-disjoint holdout; original versus column-permuted historical scores\",\n123:      \"allow_progression\": false,\n131:      \"aggregation\": \"Use each non-replay case.audit_mae for the proposed pipeline and case.baseline_audit in documented order [random_lowrank, greedy_ridge]. These already average checkpoints with the appropriate row/family weighting. Pair original and permuted points within seed and condition; show all seeds and descriptive means. This refits/tunes the complete pipeline on permuted history and is not a pure covariance-only, mixture-only, or adaptivity-only ablation.\",\n152:        \"grounded_content\": \"Document equal checkpoint weighting, equal model-row weighting for model-group, equal proxy-family means for family-disjoint, and equal case weighting over final seeds and conditions. Include seed-level paired deltas and fixed-audit versus policy-dependent remaining-target comparisons; distinguish descriptive split variability from independent-run confidence intervals.\",\n169:          \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/covariance.py\",\n170:          \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/mixture.py\",\n171:          \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/METHOD.md\"\n176:        \"grounded_content\": \"Document the pinned MTEB revision, source JSON and resource checksums, full task/language/split/primary-metric/dataset-revision column keys, fixed metric transforms, natural missingness, content/identity separation, name-based family proxies, masks determining query availability, seeds, and exact final data plans. Provide the existing program interface and dependency files, and distinguish recorded evaluator timing from unmeasured method-only compute or cost savings. Explain final-evidence hash linkage; anonymize all identifying absolute paths in public material.\",\n213:          \"results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1/src/METHOD.md\",\n243:    \"eight benchmarks are sufficient\",\n263:    \"Preserve evaluator aggregation exactly: equal checkpoint means, row means in model-group, equal name-proxy-family means in family-disjoint, then equal weighting of original non-replay cases across seeds and conditions. baseline_audit is ordered [random_lowrank, greedy_ridge]; case.losses is [proposed, historical_mean, queried_score_average, random_lowrank, greedy_ridge]. Reconstruct final metric aggregates as a local consistency check before plotting.\",\n265:    \"The family-disjoint seed 4021 is an essential adverse result; use exact values from the episode records rather than private memory or rounded copied text. Its lower ridge error is a performance comparison, not an identified validity/adaptivity failure. Discuss that family-disjoint averages need not worsen uniformly and the method is not uniformly best.\",\n269:    \"Retrospective query availability is derived from each held-out row’s recorded mask, with audit columns removed. Make this information assumption explicit. Naturally absent scores are not evaluated, so the study cannot establish recovery under arbitrary missing-not-at-random mechanisms or prospective access to every benchmark. Costs are counted in queried benchmarks, not measured CPU dollars or equal real benchmark runtime.\",\n270:    \"Family labels are name-derived lineage proxies, and identity/content checks operate on the frozen resources. Do not turn them into a guarantee of biological/architectural independence, contamination absence, or population-wide new-family validity. Results concern pinned English embedding panels, not generative LLMs, multilingual transfer, ranking recovery, or downstream model quality.\",\n271:    \"Private-only provenance: the selected source is results/ideas/02_value_adaptive_latent_mixtures_for_absolute_error_benchmark_prediction/program_1, as identified in results/best_program_manifest.json; the quadrature extension is not the frozen studied method. No downstream_study or study.* sources are supplied, so omit search winner narratives, search-to-final gain arithmetic, original-incumbent performance comparisons, and scored/unscored attempt counts.\",\n273:    \"At inspection, references.bib and references_provenance.json exist and agree on a retrieved method-oriented pool, but essential MTEB and several task-neighborhood starter titles are not present. Metadata retrieval is not evidence that a paper’s findings were read. Prefer a small relevant subset only after permitted original-source verification; safely obtain missing explicitly allowed starter sources before final drafting, without broad domain discovery or citation chasing. Do not use irrelevant retrieved references as padding or claim novelty priority from this incomplete pool. This stage performs no external retrieval.\",\n22:\\section{Introduction}\n41:\\section{Related Work}\n42:\\paragraph{Reducing evaluation and predicting performance.}\n45:\\paragraph{Incomplete matrices and latent profiles.}\n50:\\paragraph{Acquisition and absolute-loss decisions.}\n53:\\section{Method}\n54:\\subsection{Problem Setup and Evaluation Target}\n67:\\subsection{Design Rationale and Observed-Data Fitting}\n85:\\subsection{Conditional Prediction and Heterogeneous Profiles}\n106:\\subsection{Transfer-Oriented Acquisition}\n125:\\subsection{Historical Model Choice and Compared Pipelines}\n133:\\section{Experimental Setup}\n134:\\paragraph{Data and scope.}\n140:\\paragraph{Holdouts and controls.}\n148:\\paragraph{Aggregation and uncertainty.}\n157:\\section{Results}\n158:\\subsection{Aggregate Accuracy on Remaining and Common Targets}\n181:\\subsection{Budget Trade-Offs on Unchanged Targets}\n202:\\subsection{Split Variation and an Adverse Family-Disjoint Case}\n228:\\subsection{Dependence on Historical Cross-Task Alignment}\n251:\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n252:\\paragraph{What the comparison establishes.}\n255:\\paragraph{Missingness and target availability.}\n258:\\paragraph{Generalization and evidence strength.}\n261:\\paragraph{Practical interpretation.}\n264:\\section{Conclusion}\n274:\\section{Supplementary Information}\n276:\\subsection{Observed-Data Model and Numerical Settings}\n297:\\subsection{Data Provenance and Score Extraction}\n306:\\subsection{Aggregation and Evidence Replay}\n314:\\subsection{Baselines, Permutation, and Reset Controls}\n330:\\subsection{Reproducibility and Resource Scope}\n337:\\subsection{LLM Usage}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
