{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '251,273p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,90p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; tail -22 memory.md; ls global_memory/conclusions* global_memory/AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null; python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nclaims=json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\nkeys=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\{([\"'^,]+),'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\nprovkeys={ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance['references']}\nclaimkeys={key for claim in claims for key in claim.get('citation_keys',[])}\nprint('Bibliography/provenance key agreement:',keys==provkeys)\nprint('Citation keys represented in claims grounding:',len(keys & claimkeys),'of',len(keys))\nprint('Missing local reading records:',[ref['reading_record'] for ref in provenance['references'] if not Path(ref['reading_record']).is_file()])\nprint('Claim count:',len(claims))\nfor claim in claims:\n if any(word in claim.get('claim','').lower() for word in ['missingness','family','median','acquisition','ridge']):\n  if not claim.get('claim','').startswith('Literature positioning:'): print(json.dumps(claim,ensure_ascii=False)[:1050])\nfor filename in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n print('PROTECTED_SHA256',filename,hashlib.sha256(Path(filename).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '251,273p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,90p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; tail -22 memory.md; ls global_memory/conclusions* global_memory/AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null; python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\nclaims=json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\nkeys=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\{([\"'^,]+),'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\nprovkeys={ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance['references']}\nclaimkeys={key for claim in claims for key in claim.get('citation_keys',[])}\nprint('Bibliography/provenance key agreement:',keys==provkeys)\nprint('Citation keys represented in claims grounding:',len(keys & claimkeys),'of',len(keys))\nprint('Missing local reading records:',[ref['reading_record'] for ref in provenance['references'] if not Path(ref['reading_record']).is_file()])\nprint('Claim count:',len(claims))\nfor claim in claims:\n if any(word in claim.get('claim','').lower() for word in ['missingness','family','median','acquisition','ridge']):\n  if not claim.get('claim','').startswith('Literature positioning:'): print(json.dumps(claim,ensure_ascii=False)[:1050])\nfor filename in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n print('PROTECTED_SHA256',filename,hashlib.sha256(Path(filename).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n\\paragraph{What the comparison establishes.}\nThe evidence supports lower aggregate error for the frozen \\latent\\ procedure than for the two executed predictive baselines on these recorded English embedding panels. The common-target comparison strengthens this finding because scored audit cells do not change with acquisition. It remains a comparison among evaluated complete configurations. In particular, the data do not establish that mixtures were selected, that a mixture outperformed a Gaussian under matched queries, or that the square-root criterion improved over variance transfer. Their static implementation is inspectable; their individual empirical contributions are not externally verified.\n\n\\paragraph{Missingness and target availability.}\nObserved-data likelihood avoids fitting absent cells as zeros, but it does not make leaderboard missingness ignorable. Model inclusion, panel coverage, and the requirement of recorded audit scores restrict the evaluated population. The query interface assumes knowledge of which historical target entries exist; a prospective evaluator may instead be able to run different tasks or face uncertain availability. Naturally unrecorded scores remain unevaluated. Likewise, averaging normalized heterogeneous metrics is convenient for prediction error but need not match the evaluator's utility. No sensitivity study over alternative missingness mechanisms, target weights, or task-cost schedules is available.\n\n\\paragraph{Generalization and evidence strength.}\nName-derived families are proxies for lineage, and content disjointness addresses a narrower issue than architectural or training-data independence. The adverse family-disjoint split rules out a uniform advantage over the stronger baseline. Small, potentially overlapping split sets preclude strong population-level claims from the descriptive averages. A further benchmark source, multilingual coverage, larger acquisition budgets, calibrated predictive intervals, and a prospective new-model study are not measured. None should be inferred from operational qualification or the existence of a reproducible score extraction procedure. Predictions should complement direct measurement, not be relabeled as measured benchmark results.\n\n\\paragraph{Practical interpretation.}\nThe procedure is appropriate as a candidate tool when historical cross-task relationships are informative, comparable benchmark contexts can be identified, and the target resembles the represented population closely enough for conditional transfer. The observed degradation under permutation and heterogeneous split behavior provide reasons to monitor this assumption rather than assume it. A deployment should preserve a directly evaluated audit panel and expose prediction uncertainty and provenance. These are cautions motivated by the study, not capabilities validated for the present implementation.\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\nBudgeted benchmark prediction requires evaluating both a selection policy and the predictor it enables. On naturally incomplete English MTEB panels, the studied missingness-aware latent procedure obtains lower aggregate normalized absolute error than random-acquisition low-rank and greedy-coverage ridge pipelines. Its advantage persists on never-queryable audit targets, but a family-disjoint split favors ridge, and historical-column permutation substantially increases error. The appropriate conclusion is thus a bounded empirical finding about complete configurations, not uniform superiority or identification of a successful component. Within the tested budgets, additional observations improve descriptive mean audit accuracy, but the study does not determine a universally adequate number of benchmarks. Retaining common targets, adverse splits, and the distinction between recorded and naturally missing scores is essential when using such predictions to reduce evaluation effort.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics]]\n% @evidence[[derived_results.json]]\n\n\\clearpage\n\\bibliography{references}\n\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n\\clearpage\n\\appendix\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n- next_action: Add genuine source-ID provenance anchors with explicit scope, mirror the memo, and rerun strategy-only validation. Preserve the bounded English MTEB comparison over unsupported generative-model or quadrature-superiority stories.\n\n### 2026-11-13T00:02:37.113565+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper_strategy_repair_ready: both strategy files repaired; local strategy-only checks report no hard errors. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Source provenance repair does not change scientific recommendations.\n- evidence: Replaced both empty supplementary source_ids lists with existing paper-data provenance anchors and added explicit source_scope limitations. The memo mirrors the repair; implementation details remain grounded in code and LLM roles in status files/logs, never metric values. Local validation checked all six supplementary sections, twelve unique source IDs, three figure budgets, 5.5-by-9-inch single-column geometry, memo consistency, selected-implementation manifest linkage, and final episode SHA-256. Frozen English MTEB thesis, adverse split, unverified-component limits and independently completed/qualified final outcome remain unchanged. No paper drafting, external retrieval, figure generation, evaluator execution or final-paper validation occurred.\n- next_action: Writer should follow the repaired strategy and preserve descriptive comparisons, common-target audit, adverse split and incomplete mechanism attribution. Stop reason: requested strategy repair complete. Next scientific hypothesis remains the unisolated value of mixture inference or adaptive acquisition; broad generative-model and quadrature-superiority narratives remain unsupported.\n\n### 2026-11-13T00:05:33.427648+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Evidence and framing confirmed; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No new empirical recommendation.\n- evidence: final.qualification.status=completed and final.qualification.outcome=qualified, independently read. Frozen selected source is latent-mixture procedure, not quadrature; no ablations or additional tasks. Missing local apply_patch executable is bridged by a temporary patch runner outside workspace. Scientific-evidence bundle emitted.\n- next_action: Preserve readable evaluated sources, retrieve only permitted exact original references, and derive fixed-audit figures from sealed episodes.\n\n### 2026-11-13T00:22:17.078851+00:00 | step=draft | scope=paper\n- summary: Standalone draft and audit figures authored; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Derived summaries add no new empirical recommendation.\n- evidence: Final remaining MAE aggregates reproduced exactly; common-audit latent/ridge/random MAE=0.02687115/0.02940954/0.03546852. All original split cases retained, including family-disjoint seed4021 reversal. Historical tuning diagnostics remain unverified; no mechanism-specific gain claimed. Quantitative plots exported as PDF and 300-DPI PNG with provenance; overview placeholder is guarded and orchestration-owned. Official ICLR2026 template retrieved directly; its two omitted headers restored without geometry changes. An incorrect spectral-regularization DOI and unrelated EM abstract were rejected; only permitted