: [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived_results.json#/audit_budget_curves\"]}\n{\"claim\": \"Observed-data factor fitting, Gaussian conditional prediction, bounded mixture median prediction, and moment-matched off-diagonal transfer rules are implemented in the selected preserved source. Equation-level optimality applies to the fitted distribution, not real-data Bayes optimality. Dense row-state covariance storage and rank-one updates have quadratic benchmark-count complexity.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.top_program_01\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/latent/covariance.py\", \"source_evidence/latent/mixture.py\", \"source_evidence/protocol/selection_manifest.json\"], \"source_scope\": \"Registry IDs and selection manifest establish provenance; readable code is the substantive implementation evidence.\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Historical model choice uses ranks 2/4/8, residual shrinkage 2/12, optional mixture sizes 2/4, regularization 2/8, at most twelve validation/profile sweeps, thirty outer fitting sweeps, and twenty-five median bisections; the internal replacement margin is max(1e-4,0.5 paired SE). Further floors, initializations and validation dimensions are described directly from the source, not from unverified runtime diagnostics.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.top_program_01\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/latent/covariance.py\", \"source_evidence/latent/mixture.py\", \"source_evidence/protocol/evaluate_final.py#main\"], \"source_scope\": \"Static settings only; no assertion about realized component, fallback, or selector choices.\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Random low-rank uses masked alternating ridge with ranks 2/4, penalties 0.1/1, eight validation sweeps and thirty final sweeps. Greedy ridge uses overlap-shrunk correlations with at least four pairs, n/(n+10) shrinkage, and penalty 0.1.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"sourc